device_id,device_ip,vlan,svi_ip,svi_mask,guest_ip,model,platform
# One row per device — NETWORK INFO ONLY. Tokens and secrets are handled
# automatically by tools/gen-device-installers.sh (it talks to the running IRIS server).
# 'model' is OPTIONAL. Leave it blank to let Console onboarding auto-detect the
# platform (Guest Shell / IOx) from a live 'show version'; set it (e.g.
# C9300-48UXM, IE-3400) to pick the installer deterministically.
# 'platform' is OPTIONAL and LAST: blank = auto (by model), or force 'guestshell'
# or 'iox'. Set a C9300 to 'iox' to onboard it as an amd64 IOx Docker app
# (needs iris-amd64.tar staged) instead of Guest Shell.
# SDA deployment (IS-IS underlay) is assumed. svi_ip/guest_ip are a /30 at the
# back end of the device's subnet.
